 # Business Rules — PegaFila
 
-Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements. Core domain issuance is implemented via `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (ticket into an active queue) and deterministic call-next via `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (three call modes + 3-ticket fairness); HTTP, Livewire, and billing remain future work.
+Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements. Core domain issuance is implemented via `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (ticket into an active queue), deterministic call-next via `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (three call modes + 3-ticket fairness), queue management and per-queue call authorization (`CreateQueue`, `UpdateQueue`, `SetQueueAccess`, `QueuePolicy`); HTTP, Livewire, and billing remain future work.
 
 ## MVP Scope
 
@@ -98,7 +98,40 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once, authorized with the `call` ability on its queue — see [Queue management and call access](#queue-management-and-call-access)). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); every mode is authorized the same way. HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+
+### Queue management and call access
+
+Queues are managed by the entity's managers. Employees only get what a manager grants per queue.
+
+**Queue lifecycle** (`App\Actions\CreateQueue`, `App\Actions\UpdateQueue`; owner or admin of the entity only):
+
+| Operation | Rules |
+| --------- | ----- |
+| **Create** | Name is trimmed and must be 1–255 characters. Slug defaults to the slug of the name (`Atendimento Geral` → `atendimento-geral`); an explicit slug is also slugified. New queues are active. |
+| **Update** | Any combination of new name, new slug and active flag; `null` leaves a field unchanged. Keeping the queue's own slug is fine; taking another queue's slug is rejected. |
+| **Deactivate / reactivate** | `is_active = false` retires a queue. Its tickets are kept; issuing or calling on it fails with `InactiveQueueException`. |
+| **Delete** | **Not allowed.** There is no delete action for queues. |
+
+**Slug uniqueness:** unique **within an entity** (the same slug may exist in another entity). A duplicate, including one that loses a concurrent-insert race, is a validation error, not a database error.
+
+**Call permission** (`QueuePolicy::call`, ability `call`):
+
+| Caller | May call tickets on the queue |
+| ------ | ----------------------------- |
+| Owner or admin of the queue's entity | Always (no grant needed). |
+| Employee | Only with a grant on **that** queue whose permissions include `call`. |
+| Anyone else (non-member, member of another entity) | Never. |
+
+**Granting access** (`App\Actions\SetQueueAccess`; owner or admin of the queue's entity only):
+
+- A non-empty permission list grants those permissions on the queue to the membership (replacing the previous list). An empty list revokes the grant.
+- The only permission today is `call`. Unknown or non-string entries are rejected and nothing is stored.
+- The membership and the queue must belong to the same entity.
+- Employees cannot grant access, including to themselves.
+- Every grant is written to the `audit` channel as `queue.access.granted`, and every revoke as `queue.access.revoked`, each with `actor_id`, `queue_id` and `entity_membership_id`. A revoke that removes nothing is not logged.
+
+**Enforcement:** `CallNextTicket` authorizes the caller after locking the queue and checking it is active, in every call mode. `Ticket::call()` checks in this order: queue is active (`InactiveQueueException`), caller is authorized (`AuthorizationException`, even if the ticket was already called), ticket is still waiting (`LogicException`).
 
